WEBVTT

00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:09.300
After being re-built a number of times, the home of the Abh, the space fortress Ablïarsec...

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:14.420
...is still used today as the Imperial Palace.

00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:21.480
This immense fortress built to accommodate up to one million...

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:25.600
...now houses a further 200,000 Abh in its confines...

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:34.150
...turning it into a city rather than an mere orbiting palace.

00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:39.990
Envoys from other nations have arrived for what will be a turning point in history.

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:07.960
Ambassador, United Mankind

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:07.960
Sample Sangalini

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:45.730
Ïucrabé

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:45.730
To the Battlefield

00:02:58.090 --> 00:02:59.360
Vassal Sernaic...

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:01.860
...vassal Alisa...

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:05.950
...and the others whose names I do not know...

00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:11.000
...the imperial citizens who cooperated with me...

00:03:12.470 --> 00:03:14.460
<i>...I thank you very much.</i>

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:18.630
<i>I will return as soon as I can.</i>

00:03:19.850 --> 00:03:21.970
<i>I ask that you wait for me until then.</i>

00:03:25.590 --> 00:03:29.180
You still insist on going to Sfagnomr?

00:03:29.830 --> 00:03:31.430
It's my mission.

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:36.690
There's a chance you could get caught in the midst of battle.

00:03:38.330 --> 00:03:38.770
I'm going.

00:03:39.670 --> 00:03:42.030
When unsure whether to stay or go...

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:43.530
...I was taught that I should go.

00:03:45.770 --> 00:03:47.240
Farewell, young man.

00:03:48.610 --> 00:03:50.910
Come again when you have some time.

00:03:51.510 --> 00:03:54.540
I want to hear all about how the Haïder family came to be.

00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:59.550
In return, I'll give you all there is to know about the Abh.

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:02.090
I'd like that.

00:04:02.690 --> 00:04:05.880
If possible, before you have children.

00:04:06.460 --> 00:04:07.090
Sure.

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:11.390
We loaded up on fuel...

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:14.350
...bid farewell to the Baron...

00:04:15.270 --> 00:04:17.600
...and left the Feubdach domain.

00:04:18.910 --> 00:04:23.400
We headed for what was likely a battlefield.

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:29.660
Jinto.

00:04:30.650 --> 00:04:33.450
The gates to Sfagnomr show on our range navigator.

00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:35.210
What's the situation?

00:04:35.890 --> 00:04:37.540
There are a number of space-time bubbles.

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:40.000
I don't know if they're enemies or allies.

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:41.800
What if they're enemies?

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:43.630
We'll force our way through.

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:46.800
Naturally.

00:04:47.140 --> 00:04:50.800
I expect we'll enter the Sfagnomr gates in 7 hours.

00:04:51.740 --> 00:04:54.560
I hope they'll welcome us warmly.

00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:58.060
They may welcome us with intense fire.

00:05:02.950 --> 00:05:03.490
Jinto...

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:05.760
...I've got bad news.

00:05:06.360 --> 00:05:07.290
I figured.

00:05:08.290 --> 00:05:10.260
Don't tell me any more.

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:13.540
A signal's trying to determine whether we're friend or foe.

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:14.830
From the Empire?

00:05:16.030 --> 00:05:17.440
I don't know whose signal it is...

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:20.570
...but I know it's not the Empire's.

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:23.290
Can't we deceive them?

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:25.050
Make it look like we're allies?

00:05:26.310 --> 00:05:28.550
How can you think of such distasteful tactics?

00:05:29.950 --> 00:05:31.930
Must be my upbringing.

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:34.220
That's it.

00:05:35.350 --> 00:05:35.890
What is?

00:05:36.450 --> 00:05:37.430
An order to stop the ship.

00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:41.310
They say that unless we come to a halt, they'll attack us.

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:45.320
Of course, you're not about to stop, are you?

00:05:46.130 --> 00:05:47.320
Do you want me to stop?

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:48.780
No.

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:51.120
Let's go, then.

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:00.330
Did we avoid them?!

00:06:02.710 --> 00:06:04.130
Don't follow us!

00:06:05.250 --> 00:06:06.170
I'll try to lose them.

00:06:06.650 --> 00:06:07.300
Can you do that?

00:06:07.750 --> 00:06:09.220
We can if the mines run out of fuel.

00:06:09.850 --> 00:06:11.430
What about our fuel?

00:06:12.490 --> 00:06:13.300
Please, God...

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:17.680
There's more!

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:21.100
Who in the world ordered extra mines!

00:06:21.660 --> 00:06:23.310
We might be able to beat them.

00:06:23.630 --> 00:06:24.020
Huh?!

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:25.860
The mines are almost out of fuel...

00:06:26.600 --> 00:06:28.110
...so they deployed more mines.

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:30.900
All right!

00:06:31.770 --> 00:06:32.660
But...

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:34.120
We're okay!

00:06:35.180 --> 00:06:35.980
We can make it!

00:06:47.360 --> 00:06:49.050
They're coming, Lafiel.

00:06:50.290 --> 00:06:51.470
Going to battle speed.

00:06:58.970 --> 00:07:02.940
I bet they'll chase us right to normal space!

00:07:05.650 --> 00:07:08.940
Our speed capability in normal space is better than theirs is!

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:20.750
We made it.

00:07:21.360 --> 00:07:22.210
And the mines?

00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:23.460
They're there.

00:07:27.930 --> 00:07:30.510
They misjudged where we'd come out.

00:07:34.940 --> 00:07:38.310
But won't the enemy be in this area as well?

00:07:38.610 --> 00:07:40.350
I don't think so.

00:07:41.910 --> 00:07:43.310
It hardly makes sense.

00:07:44.180 --> 00:07:45.650
They're too busy with other things.

00:07:46.360 --> 00:07:47.020
Look over there.

00:07:53.260 --> 00:07:54.740
The enemy in planar space...

00:07:55.360 --> 00:07:57.950
...wasn't seeking out Laburec coming from afar.

00:07:58.690 --> 00:08:00.620
They were blockading Sfagnomr.

00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:03.580
They're in the midst of a battle.

00:08:05.730 --> 00:08:07.880
Imperial Laburec, please respond.

00:08:08.370 --> 00:08:11.210
This is a transfer shuttle from the patrol ship Gosroth.

00:08:14.480 --> 00:08:16.470
Imperial Laburec, please respond.

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:21.220
Imperial Laburec, please respond.

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:25.730
Imperial Laburec, please respond.

00:08:28.990 --> 00:08:31.230
<i>This is Sufagnoff communications base.</i>

00:08:31.890 --> 00:08:34.030
<i>What is your status, transfer shuttle?</i>

00:08:35.900 --> 00:08:37.820
The patrol ship Gosroth encountered...

00:08:37.820 --> 00:08:42.450
...unidentified space-time bubbles in Area Itoum 533.

00:08:46.010 --> 00:08:48.460
We arrived here...

00:08:48.740 --> 00:08:51.840
...ahead of the mothership with its logbook and a civilian.

00:08:52.580 --> 00:08:54.670
We are arriving at your base.

00:08:55.980 --> 00:08:56.590
<i>Roger.</i>

00:08:57.250 --> 00:08:57.970
<i>Transfer shuttle.</i>

00:08:58.590 --> 00:09:00.050
<i>Due to military secrecy...</i>

00:09:00.050 --> 00:09:02.770
<i>...you are prohibited from further communication.</i>

00:09:03.330 --> 00:09:03.890
Roger.

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:05.520
Sfagnomr base.

00:09:06.130 --> 00:09:06.940
Your instructions please.

00:09:08.030 --> 00:09:10.400
<i>Unfortunately, we cannot allow your shuttle to enter the base.</i>

00:09:11.130 --> 00:09:12.230
<i>Proceed on your own.</i>

00:09:13.870 --> 00:09:14.610
Roger.

00:09:15.270 --> 00:09:16.240
Sfagnomr Base.

00:09:16.910 --> 00:09:19.200
From here on in, we will proceed on our own.

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:20.740
Good luck.

00:09:22.540 --> 00:09:25.120
<i>That's small comfort, transfer shuttle.</i>

00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:28.040
<i>But may the Empire be victorious.</i>

00:09:31.630 --> 00:09:33.420
Does that mean they're about to lose?

00:09:34.210 --> 00:09:35.260
Of course.

00:09:35.960 --> 00:09:38.470
There's limited personnel stationed in the colonies.

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:43.640
One base won't likely withstand a full assault.

00:09:45.390 --> 00:09:46.270
Sorry.

00:09:47.540 --> 00:09:49.100
That was a stupid question.

00:09:49.770 --> 00:09:50.400
It's okay.

00:09:53.650 --> 00:09:54.730
I'm sorry, Jinto.

00:09:55.280 --> 00:09:59.150
I failed to safely get you to your destination after all.

00:10:00.480 --> 00:10:01.820
It's not your fault.

00:10:02.650 --> 00:10:04.830
What's the status with the enemy?

00:10:05.490 --> 00:10:06.200
They're far.

00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:09.040
But three vessels are headed this way.

00:10:09.590 --> 00:10:10.370
Three...

00:10:10.370 --> 00:10:13.720
Those guys really like the number three, don't they.

00:10:15.600 --> 00:10:16.460
What could that be?

00:10:19.170 --> 00:10:20.470
Looks like a space elevator.

00:10:22.510 --> 00:10:24.850
It's been destroyed by the enemy.

00:10:26.110 --> 00:10:27.390
What a lowly thing to do.

00:10:28.210 --> 00:10:30.350
Space elevators are not military bases.

00:10:31.380 --> 00:10:31.810
Hey.

00:10:32.600 --> 00:10:35.320
Is this shuttle able to land?

00:10:35.320 --> 00:10:36.070
Land?

00:10:36.480 --> 00:10:37.110
That's right.

00:10:37.860 --> 00:10:40.700
If there're no space elevators, we have no choice but to land.

00:10:41.820 --> 00:10:42.740
We should be able to.

00:10:45.890 --> 00:10:46.870
"Should?"

00:10:50.430 --> 00:10:52.830
Yup. It looks like we can.

00:10:53.290 --> 00:10:54.290
Wait a minute.

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:58.460
Are you telling me you weren't even thinking of landing this ship?

00:10:58.760 --> 00:10:59.260
No.

00:10:59.980 --> 00:11:01.630
Then what were you planning to do?

00:11:02.180 --> 00:11:03.840
I thought I'd take part in the battle.

00:11:04.210 --> 00:11:05.100
But how?!

00:11:05.550 --> 00:11:06.970
This shuttle isn't even armed.

00:11:07.820 --> 00:11:09.100
I wasn't thinking about that.

00:11:09.880 --> 00:11:10.350
But...

00:11:11.220 --> 00:11:13.310
...you never know, there might be something.

00:11:13.990 --> 00:11:16.690
Even now, we've got three enemy vessels on our tail.

00:11:16.820 --> 00:11:18.610
You fool!

00:11:22.320 --> 00:11:24.110
I'll just have to accept whatever you say.

00:11:24.930 --> 00:11:27.330
I did trivialize your life.

00:11:27.940 --> 00:11:29.370
Your own life, too.

00:11:33.640 --> 00:11:37.000
You people are able to live a much longer life.

00:11:37.280 --> 00:11:39.000
Why are you in a hurry to die?

00:11:39.510 --> 00:11:41.090
We're not necessarily hurrying to die.

00:11:41.950 --> 00:11:43.300
It sure looks that way.

00:11:44.220 --> 00:11:45.800
The battle has already begun.

00:11:46.660 --> 00:11:49.680
When a soldier goes to battle, there's only one thing to do.

00:11:50.090 --> 00:11:51.350
Then do as you wish.

00:11:52.290 --> 00:11:54.900
But I'm not a soldier yet.

00:11:55.690 --> 00:11:57.230
Let me off at this planet first.

00:11:57.860 --> 00:11:58.610
Okay.

00:11:59.230 --> 00:12:02.820
You're of no use in the battle anyway.

00:12:03.540 --> 00:12:05.030
Neither are you.

00:12:09.710 --> 00:12:10.540
Sorry.

00:12:11.280 --> 00:12:12.830
You're absolutely right.

00:12:13.520 --> 00:12:14.210
I know...

00:12:16.420 --> 00:12:17.710
...I'm useless.

00:12:18.890 --> 00:12:19.990
I told you before.

00:12:21.160 --> 00:12:23.630
You're a great help to me.

00:12:28.730 --> 00:12:32.370
You see, I may be useless right now...

00:12:33.330 --> 00:12:36.740
...but someday, someone might be able to rely on me.

00:12:37.810 --> 00:12:39.580
I'd like to live until then...

00:12:40.280 --> 00:12:42.650
...and I'd also like you to live until then.

00:12:43.650 --> 00:12:44.150
Yeah.

00:12:46.410 --> 00:12:47.320
Is it the base?

00:12:47.870 --> 00:12:48.450
No.

00:12:48.980 --> 00:12:50.870
The signal's coming from the spaceship ahead.

00:12:51.550 --> 00:12:52.330
The enemy...

00:12:52.870 --> 00:12:53.410
Are they close?

00:12:53.750 --> 00:12:55.210
Yes. Very.

00:12:55.920 --> 00:12:58.670
They're saying they'll open fire unless we stop.

00:12:59.660 --> 00:13:02.210
I was hoping they'd say something more interesting.

00:13:03.460 --> 00:13:06.630
I wouldn't want to be killed by uninteresting people.

00:13:07.220 --> 00:13:07.970
Neither would I.

00:13:10.210 --> 00:13:13.310
Then let's hurry onto that planet.

00:13:14.110 --> 00:13:15.560
We'll have to elude them first.

00:13:25.890 --> 00:13:26.820
Are we safe now?

00:13:27.460 --> 00:13:30.700
Even if they changed directions now, they couldn't catch up with us.

00:13:32.290 --> 00:13:33.660
We're entering the atmosphere.

00:13:34.760 --> 00:13:36.080
Try and stay calm.

00:13:37.410 --> 00:13:38.860
Try and be gentle.

00:13:45.740 --> 00:13:47.220
What? What's the matter?

00:13:47.810 --> 00:13:48.840
Don't worry.

00:13:49.310 --> 00:13:51.010
I just jettisoned the main engine.

00:13:51.510 --> 00:13:52.760
What do you mean "just?!"

00:13:53.140 --> 00:13:57.730
We can't enter the atmosphere loaded with anti-matter fuel.

00:13:58.550 --> 00:14:00.440
We have to think of the inhabitants.

00:14:01.290 --> 00:14:01.860
But...

00:14:03.560 --> 00:14:06.990
This transfer shuttle isn't designed for landing.

00:14:07.700 --> 00:14:11.030
So a landing is no different than an emergency escape.

00:14:17.610 --> 00:14:19.500
Are we really okay?

00:14:20.110 --> 00:14:21.290
I'm just as scared.

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:23.000
It's my first time.

00:14:28.150 --> 00:14:29.550
It's your first time?

00:14:30.080 --> 00:14:31.090
I told you before.

00:14:32.090 --> 00:14:34.010
I've never been on a surface world.

00:14:34.720 --> 00:14:36.390
But you must have been trained?

00:14:36.390 --> 00:14:37.060
I did train!

00:14:37.690 --> 00:14:38.850
Which scares you more...

00:14:39.290 --> 00:14:41.560
...landing, or the world?!

00:14:42.160 --> 00:14:43.020
Both!

00:15:11.730 --> 00:15:13.390
Have we landed?

00:15:13.800 --> 00:15:14.430
Yeah.

00:15:17.600 --> 00:15:18.720
Jinto, let's hurry.

00:15:19.130 --> 00:15:20.850
They may be watching from above.

00:15:37.820 --> 00:15:38.370
Open.

00:15:42.020 --> 00:15:42.920
You shall hold this.

00:15:43.960 --> 00:15:44.380
Yeah.

00:15:54.340 --> 00:15:54.800
All set?

00:15:55.440 --> 00:15:55.890
All set.

00:15:56.800 --> 00:15:57.810
Prepare to self-destruct.

00:16:03.080 --> 00:16:05.350
<i>Ready for self-destruct.</i>

00:16:05.780 --> 00:16:08.320
Good-bye. Begin self-destruct.

00:16:08.980 --> 00:16:09.610
<i>Acknowledged.</i>

00:16:10.420 --> 00:16:15.160
<i>In accordance with the secrecy regulations, all information and recorded transactions shall be deleted.</i>

00:16:16.490 --> 00:16:17.780
<i>I pray for your safety.</i>

00:16:21.160 --> 00:16:23.210
What a sarcastic machine.

00:16:27.440 --> 00:16:28.670
Now, let's go.

00:16:45.190 --> 00:16:45.770
What's wrong?

00:16:46.590 --> 00:16:48.020
No, it's nothing.

00:17:04.510 --> 00:17:06.290
Jinto. Wait a minute.

00:17:07.280 --> 00:17:07.960
What's the matter?

00:17:09.010 --> 00:17:09.670
Jinto.

00:17:11.610 --> 00:17:13.590
There's something wrong with my eyes.

00:17:14.050 --> 00:17:14.970
What?

00:17:15.760 --> 00:17:16.630
The stars...

00:17:18.290 --> 00:17:19.470
...look like they're flickering.

00:17:19.850 --> 00:17:20.260
Huh?

00:17:23.260 --> 00:17:24.890
I don't want to hold you back.

00:17:26.030 --> 00:17:27.230
Should I go blind...

00:17:28.060 --> 00:17:29.480
...please take this logbook...

00:17:30.530 --> 00:17:31.940
...and proceed without me.

00:17:39.070 --> 00:17:40.040
Lafiel...

00:17:41.030 --> 00:17:44.870
...I hate to rain on that spirit of self-sacrifice of yours...

00:17:46.150 --> 00:17:49.540
...but stars twinkle when you see them through the atmosphere.

00:17:52.020 --> 00:17:53.920
Does it look the same to you too?

00:17:54.340 --> 00:17:54.840
Yeah.

00:17:55.590 --> 00:17:56.340
Really?!

00:17:56.920 --> 00:17:58.880
Why should I want to lie about it...

00:17:59.460 --> 00:18:00.300
...in a place like this?

00:18:09.670 --> 00:18:10.560
I see.

00:18:15.070 --> 00:18:16.070
You know...

00:18:17.110 --> 00:18:18.820
...I'm beginning to see quite a lot of bias...

00:18:19.410 --> 00:18:22.030
...in the education you've received.

00:18:22.580 --> 00:18:23.530
Shut up, Jinto.

00:18:39.720 --> 00:18:41.510
We slept overnight in a cave...

00:18:42.010 --> 00:18:44.390
...and when I woke up, it was already evening.

00:18:46.850 --> 00:18:52.440
<i>Praise the United Mankind for your liberation from the reign of the Humankind Empire Abh.</i>

00:18:53.380 --> 00:18:55.230
The area was very quiet.

00:18:56.020 --> 00:18:58.240
No sign of war anywhere.

00:18:58.990 --> 00:18:59.610
However...

00:19:01.160 --> 00:19:04.070
<i>This is a message from the United Mankind.</i>

00:19:08.790 --> 00:19:16.050
<i>Our reason for coming to Sfagnomr is to retaliate against the belligerent actions of the Abh.</i>

00:19:16.540 --> 00:19:17.380
I knew it.

00:19:19.740 --> 00:19:24.800
<i>While we were scanning the planar space surrounding a newly discovered saudec...</i>

00:19:25.450 --> 00:19:28.640
<i>...an Imperial warship suddenly opened fire on us.</i>

00:19:28.950 --> 00:19:29.640
That's a lie!

00:19:32.600 --> 00:19:36.270
27th Empress of the Abh Empire

00:19:32.600 --> 00:19:36.270
Lamï

00:19:32.940 --> 00:19:33.850
Ambassador

00:19:34.560 --> 00:19:36.570
It is clear that you are lying.

00:19:36.900 --> 00:19:37.520
Lying?

00:19:38.560 --> 00:19:43.030
You have stated that our warship opened fire...

00:19:43.500 --> 00:19:45.200
...but there is not one outlaw...

00:19:45.530 --> 00:19:49.580
...in our proud Laburec who would challenge anyone to battle without just cause.

00:19:51.440 --> 00:19:52.870
It was an exception.

00:19:54.110 --> 00:19:55.830
That's how we should look at it.

00:19:56.840 --> 00:19:57.670
Obviously.

00:19:58.880 --> 00:20:03.800
If it were such an exception, the ship would not have lost.

00:20:04.680 --> 00:20:07.550
<i>We were able to drive back this warship...</i>

00:20:08.190 --> 00:20:11.140
<i>...but we cannot tolerate such an attack without warning.</i>

00:20:13.230 --> 00:20:16.860
<i>We therefore have occupied Sfagnomr...</i>

00:20:17.400 --> 00:20:22.240
<i>...the closest nation, as retaliation and to ensure our safety around the new saudec.</i>

00:20:22.970 --> 00:20:25.990
What if it's Gosroth they're talking about?

00:20:27.640 --> 00:20:28.580
Ambassador.

00:20:29.940 --> 00:20:34.870
I had great expectations that you would be more tactful.

00:20:35.750 --> 00:20:37.330
I'm quite disappointed.

00:20:38.120 --> 00:20:39.290
It's too bad.

00:20:41.020 --> 00:20:43.630
Investigate this matter properly before jumping to conclusions.

00:20:44.760 --> 00:20:47.890
I suggest that we form a joint investigation committee...

00:20:48.530 --> 00:20:51.890
...between the Abh Empire and the United Mankind...

00:20:52.520 --> 00:20:56.730
...and select members from the three neutral nations.

00:20:57.840 --> 00:21:00.320
Are you also lying to me?

00:21:01.240 --> 00:21:03.690
You have formed an alliance with each other.

00:21:04.410 --> 00:21:06.070
That makes you far from being neutral.

00:21:06.450 --> 00:21:07.240
However!

00:21:11.650 --> 00:21:12.370
Your Majesty.

00:21:13.290 --> 00:21:16.710
Should you declare war against the United Mankind...

00:21:17.360 --> 00:21:19.630
...we, the People's Sovereign Union of the Planets...

00:21:20.190 --> 00:21:21.920
...in accordance with the Nova Sicily Treaty...

00:21:22.600 --> 00:21:24.340
...must declare war against you.

00:21:25.260 --> 00:21:26.510
I'm aware of that.

00:21:27.340 --> 00:21:31.770
I'm sure the Republic of Alcont and Hania feel the same.

00:21:33.180 --> 00:21:33.970
All right...

00:21:34.880 --> 00:21:36.100
...then let's go to war.

00:21:40.580 --> 00:21:41.400
Your Majesty!

00:21:42.020 --> 00:21:43.320
Please think this over.

00:21:43.880 --> 00:21:48.360
Please realize that you will be at war with half of humankind.

00:21:49.110 --> 00:21:50.910
Have you forgotten, Ambassador?

00:21:51.690 --> 00:21:54.540
The other half belongs to this Empire.

00:21:55.500 --> 00:21:57.250
I'll tell you this much.

00:21:57.730 --> 00:21:59.920
The Empire lacks the faith in a higher being.

00:22:00.430 --> 00:22:02.840
There is no way you can win.

00:22:03.710 --> 00:22:04.960
You're right.

00:22:05.610 --> 00:22:07.720
Our Empire does lack a god.

00:22:08.940 --> 00:22:09.680
However...

00:22:10.610 --> 00:22:14.560
...I doubt that divine faith has anything to do with winning.

00:22:17.290 --> 00:22:18.770
That must be superstition.

00:22:21.890 --> 00:22:23.940
Thank you all for coming.

00:22:24.960 --> 00:22:26.610
I hope you have a safe return.

00:22:27.090 --> 00:22:31.530
Your diplomatic privileges will be revoked in 24 hours.

00:22:33.130 --> 00:22:34.490
Finally, one more thing.

00:22:35.400 --> 00:22:37.410
Should we win this battle...

00:22:37.840 --> 00:22:40.250
...it will become the last war of humankind.

00:22:40.840 --> 00:22:42.170
Permanent peace?

00:22:43.080 --> 00:22:45.250
People have dreamed of it for ages...

00:22:45.810 --> 00:22:49.510
...but it has never been a reality.

00:22:50.720 --> 00:22:51.640
But remember...

00:22:52.090 --> 00:22:54.470
...there were no Abh in the past.

00:22:55.460 --> 00:22:56.600
Above our heads...

00:22:57.560 --> 00:22:58.770
...far away in outer space...

00:22:59.760 --> 00:23:04.190
...a war had officially begun.

00:24:30.420 --> 00:24:30.740
Fool.

00:24:31.350 --> 00:24:31.790
Lafiel.

00:24:32.620 --> 00:24:35.120
I'll be back as soon as possible, so wait here.

00:24:38.160 --> 00:24:39.380
Besides...

00:24:40.130 --> 00:24:41.040
...you stand out too much.

00:24:49.500 --> 00:24:50.930
Don't overdo it.

00:24:51.740 --> 00:24:55.890
"You're the only one within 100 light years that I can trust."

00:24:56.390 --> 00:24:56.980
Yeah, right...

00:24:57.230 --> 00:24:59.810
Escape: Just the Two of Us

00:24:57.230 --> 00:24:59.810
Digecauth Matnir Latta

00:24:57.850 --> 00:24:59.480
Like she'd ever say anything like that.
